---
---
<lem-type Note extends Page>
  topic: string
  title: string = "TIL: " + self.topic
  slug: string = path
  hero: Photo? by site.photos
  layout: (Note, html): html = note
</lem-type>

<lem-fn note(n: Note, body: html)>
  <h1><lem.n.title></h1>
  <lem.body>
</lem-fn>

A default is checked against its field and sees the record being built as `self`, and
a page's `path` and `body` besides; a `by` index resolves a string in front matter
through a map on `site`; `layout` defaults to a function of the schema's own type. All
of it runs at load, none of it at render.
